  "title": "Forebrain Acsl4 loss induces an SREBP2 sterol-compensation program that is absent from thalamic and midbrain classes",
  "status": "grounded",
  "rejection_reason": null,
  "exact_observed_result": "Partial Acsl4 depletion induced a small FDR-supported SREBP2/sterol program in forebrain glutamatergic classes, with the genes moving opposite to direct Srebf2 perturbation; high-powered thalamic and midbrain classes depleted Acsl4 without inducing the module.",
  "biological_interpretation": "Neuronal ACSL4 loss engages a forebrain-enriched lipid feedback loop rather than a knockdown-strength-dictated sterol response.",
